@lang en
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ito-il30-nouns`
IMPORT `ito-64a1-transparent-company`

-- Tests for s 64A1 (the transparent company). Expected values were worked by hand from the section before they were run. All figures are HYPOTHETICAL.

§ `Tests of section 64A1`

§§ `Fixtures`

-- A company that meets all eight conditions, with 10 shareholders and the regulations in force.
`a company that meets every condition` MEANS
    `A company that may be transparent` WITH
        `the company is resident in Israel` IS TRUE
        `the company is a public company as defined in section 1 of the Companies Law, or its articles allow it to become one` IS FALSE
        `the number of shareholders, counting spouses and their children, heirs of a shareholder, and buyers from a shareholder in an involuntary sale, as one` IS 10
        `the Director approved a higher number of shareholders, up to` IS NOTHING
        `every shareholder is an individual resident in Israel` IS TRUE
        `the shares are all of one type except for voting rights, and the shareholders cannot change the rights the shares carry except voting rights` IS TRUE
        `the right to the company's profits comes from the shares alone` IS TRUE
        `each shareholder's right to profits is the same as his right to the company's assets on winding up` IS TRUE
        `the company is a financial institution as defined in the Value Added Tax Law` IS FALSE
        `the company asked to be a transparent company by a notice signed by all its shareholders and delivered to the assessing officer within 60 days of its incorporation` IS TRUE
        `regulations under section 64A1 are in force` IS TRUE

GIVEN res   IS A BOOLEAN
      pub   IS A BOOLEAN
      n     IS A NUMBER
      appr  IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      indiv IS A BOOLEAN
      oneclass IS A BOOLEAN
      profits  IS A BOOLEAN
      equal    IS A BOOLEAN
      fin   IS A BOOLEAN
      asked IS A BOOLEAN
      regs  IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `A company that may be transparent`
`a company:` res `, public` pub `, shareholders` n `, approved up to` appr `, all resident individuals` indiv `, one class` oneclass `, profits by shares` profits `, equal rights` equal `, financial institution` fin `, asked in time` asked `, regulations in force` regs MEANS
    `A company that may be transparent` WITH
        `the company is resident in Israel` IS res
        `the company is a public company as defined in section 1 of the Companies Law, or its articles allow it to become one` IS pub
        `the number of shareholders, counting spouses and their children, heirs of a shareholder, and buyers from a shareholder in an involuntary sale, as one` IS n
        `the Director approved a higher number of shareholders, up to` IS appr
        `every shareholder is an individual resident in Israel` IS indiv
        `the shares are all of one type except for voting rights, and the shareholders cannot change the rights the shares carry except voting rights` IS oneclass
        `the right to the company's profits comes from the shares alone` IS profits
        `each shareholder's right to profits is the same as his right to the company's assets on winding up` IS equal
        `the company is a financial institution as defined in the Value Added Tax Law` IS fin
        `the company asked to be a transparent company by a notice signed by all its shareholders and delivered to the assessing officer within 60 days of its incorporation` IS asked
        `regulations under section 64A1 are in force` IS regs

GIVEN f IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `A shareholder of a transparent company`
`a shareholder with the profit share of` f MEANS
    `A shareholder of a transparent company` WITH
        `the fraction of the right to profits` IS f
        `the company's income of the year that is exempt from tax` IS 0

§§ `Paragraph (a): the eight conditions`
#ASSERT `s 64A1(a) — the company is a transparent company` `a company that meets every condition`
-- Each condition failing in turn.
#ASSERT NOT `s 64A1(a) — the company is a transparent company` (`a company:` FALSE `, public` FALSE `, shareholders` 10 `, approved up to` NOTHING `, all resident individuals` TRUE `, one class` TRUE `, profits by shares` TRUE `, equal rights` TRUE `, financial institution` FALSE `, asked in time` TRUE `, regulations in force` TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `s 64A1(a) — the company is a transparent company` (`a company:` TRUE `, public` TRUE `, shareholders` 10 `, approved up to` NOTHING `, all resident individuals` TRUE `, one class` TRUE `, profits by shares` TRUE `, equal rights` TRUE `, financial institution` FALSE `, asked in time` TRUE `, regulations in force` TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `s 64A1(a) — the company is a transparent company` (`a company:` TRUE `, public` FALSE `, shareholders` 10 `, approved up to` NOTHING `, all resident individuals` FALSE `, one class` TRUE `, profits by shares` TRUE `, equal rights` TRUE `, financial institution` FALSE `, asked in time` TRUE `, regulations in force` TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `s 64A1(a) — the company is a transparent company` (`a company:` TRUE `, public` FALSE `, shareholders` 10 `, approved up to` NOTHING `, all resident individuals` TRUE `, one class` FALSE `, profits by shares` TRUE `, equal rights` TRUE `, financial institution` FALSE `, asked in time` TRUE `, regulations in force` TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `s 64A1(a) — the company is a transparent company` (`a company:` TRUE `, public` FALSE `, shareholders` 10 `, approved up to` NOTHING `, all resident individuals` TRUE `, one class` TRUE `, profits by shares` FALSE `, equal rights` TRUE `, financial institution` FALSE `, asked in time` TRUE `, regulations in force` TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `s 64A1(a) — the company is a transparent company` (`a company:` TRUE `, public` FALSE `, shareholders` 10 `, approved up to` NOTHING `, all resident individuals` TRUE `, one class` TRUE `, profits by shares` TRUE `, equal rights` FALSE `, financial institution` FALSE `, asked in time` TRUE `, regulations in force` TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `s 64A1(a) — the company is a transparent company` (`a company:` TRUE `, public` FALSE `, shareholders` 10 `, approved up to` NOTHING `, all resident individuals` TRUE `, one class` TRUE `, profits by shares` TRUE `, equal rights` TRUE `, financial institution` TRUE `, asked in time` TRUE `, regulations in force` TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `s 64A1(a) — the company is a transparent company` (`a company:` TRUE `, public` FALSE `, shareholders` 10 `, approved up to` NOTHING `, all resident individuals` TRUE `, one class` TRUE `, profits by shares` TRUE `, equal rights` TRUE `, financial institution` FALSE `, asked in time` FALSE `, regulations in force` TRUE)
-- The number of shareholders: 50 is allowed; 51 is not without the Director's approval; 51 with approval up to 60 is; 61 with approval up to 60 is not.
#ASSERT `s 64A1(a) — the company is a transparent company` (`a company:` TRUE `, public` FALSE `, shareholders` 50 `, approved up to` NOTHING `, all resident individuals` TRUE `, one class` TRUE `, profits by shares` TRUE `, equal rights` TRUE `, financial institution` FALSE `, asked in time` TRUE `, regulations in force` TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `s 64A1(a) — the company is a transparent company` (`a company:` TRUE `, public` FALSE `, shareholders` 51 `, approved up to` NOTHING `, all resident individuals` TRUE `, one class` TRUE `, profits by shares` TRUE `, equal rights` TRUE `, financial institution` FALSE `, asked in time` TRUE `, regulations in force` TRUE)
#ASSERT `s 64A1(a) — the company is a transparent company` (`a company:` TRUE `, public` FALSE `, shareholders` 51 `, approved up to` (JUST 60) `, all resident individuals` TRUE `, one class` TRUE `, profits by shares` TRUE `, equal rights` TRUE `, financial institution` FALSE `, asked in time` TRUE `, regulations in force` TRUE)
#ASSERT `s 64A1(a) — the company is a transparent company` (`a company:` TRUE `, public` FALSE `, shareholders` 60 `, approved up to` (JUST 60) `, all resident individuals` TRUE `, one class` TRUE `, profits by shares` TRUE `, equal rights` TRUE `, financial institution` FALSE `, asked in time` TRUE `, regulations in force` TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `s 64A1(a) — the company is a transparent company` (`a company:` TRUE `, public` FALSE `, shareholders` 61 `, approved up to` (JUST 60) `, all resident individuals` TRUE `, one class` TRUE `, profits by shares` TRUE `, equal rights` TRUE `, financial institution` FALSE `, asked in time` TRUE `, regulations in force` TRUE)
-- The regulations not in force (or not shown): declined.
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 64A1(a) — the company is a transparent company` (`a company:` TRUE `, public` FALSE `, shareholders` 10 `, approved up to` NOTHING `, all resident individuals` TRUE `, one class` TRUE `, profits by shares` TRUE `, equal rights` TRUE `, financial institution` FALSE `, asked in time` TRUE `, regulations in force` FALSE) BECAUSE "section 64A1 applies from the day regulations under it come into force, and whether they are in force is not shown by the sources"

§§ `Paragraph (b): attribution and the arithmetic of the sale of a share`
-- 100,000 of taxable income, a 30% right to profits: 30,000.
#ASSERT `s 64A1(b) — the part of the income of` 100_000 `attributed to the shareholder with` (`a shareholder with the profit share of` (30%)) EQUALS 30_000
-- Profits distributed: 100,000 + 10,000 - 5,000 = 105,000.
#ASSERT `s 64A1(b)(2) — the profits distributed from` 100_000 `with the exempt income` 10_000 `less the tax the company paid and did not charge:` 5_000 EQUALS 105_000
-- Losses: 8,000 attributed, 5,000 of income from the company: 5,000 set off ; 3,000 of loss, 5,000 of income: 3,000.
#ASSERT `s 64A1(b)(3)(a) — the loss set off against the shareholder's income from the company, of` 8_000 `against` 5_000 EQUALS 5_000
#ASSERT `s 64A1(b)(3)(a) — the loss set off against the shareholder's income from the company, of` 3_000 `against` 5_000 EQUALS 3_000
-- The active role: personal-exertion income only if the company's income is such and the shareholder had an active role.
#ASSERT `s 64A1(b)(4) — the shareholder's share is personal-exertion income when the company's income is such:` TRUE `and the shareholder's active role:` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 64A1(b)(4) — the shareholder's share is personal-exertion income when the company's income is such:` TRUE `and the shareholder's active role:` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `s 64A1(b)(4) — the shareholder's share is personal-exertion income when the company's income is such:` FALSE `and the shareholder's active role:` TRUE
-- Foreign tax 2,000, a 25% right: 500.
#ASSERT `s 64A1(b)(5) — the shareholder's share of the foreign tax` 2_000 `for` (`a shareholder with the profit share of` (25%)) EQUALS 500
-- On the sale of a 40% share, undistributed profits of 200,000 in the benefit years: the reduction 80,000.
#ASSERT `s 64A1(b)(8)(a) — the reduction for the sale of the share of` (`a shareholder with the profit share of` (40%)) `from the undistributed profits` 200_000 EQUALS 80_000
-- "Profits": taxable income 50,000 less losses 70,000: not negative, so 0 ; taxable income 50,000 less losses 20,000: 30,000.
#ASSERT `s 64A1(b)(8)(a) — the profits of the benefit years` 50_000 `less the losses` 70_000 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `s 64A1(b)(8)(a) — the profits of the benefit years` 50_000 `less the losses` 20_000 EQUALS 30_000
-- The seller's adjusted original price 100,000 less losses attributed 30,000: 70,000 ; less losses 150,000, up to the price: 0.
#ASSERT `s 64A1(b)(8)(c) — the adjusted original price` 100_000 `less the losses attributed to the seller:` 30_000 EQUALS 70_000
#ASSERT `s 64A1(b)(8)(c) — the adjusted original price` 100_000 `less the losses attributed to the seller:` 150_000 EQUALS 0
-- The seller notifies within 90 days of the sale: a sale on 1 March 2026: 30 May 2026.
#ASSERT `s 64A1(b)(9) — the last day for the seller to notify the company of the sale on` (YMD 2026 3 1) EQUALS YMD 2026 5 30
-- Winding-up: an asset worth 1,000,000 transferred in proportion with its use unchanged and no betterment tax charged: purchase tax 0.5% = 5,000 ; otherwise this paragraph imposes none.
#ASSERT `s 64A1(b)(11)(a) — the purchase tax on the transfer of an asset worth` 1_000_000 `on winding-up:` TRUE `and betterment tax is not charged:` TRUE EQUALS 5_000
#ASSERT `s 64A1(b)(11)(a) — the purchase tax on the transfer of an asset worth` 1_000_000 `on winding-up:` TRUE `and betterment tax is not charged:` FALSE EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `s 64A1(b)(11)(a) — the purchase tax on the transfer of an asset worth` 1_000_000 `on winding-up:` FALSE `and betterment tax is not charged:` TRUE EQUALS 0

§§ `Paragraph (d)(1): the last day to assess the shareholder`
-- The company's assessment made in tax year 2026: two years from its end is 31 December 2028. The shareholder's income assessable from 1 June 2029: the later, 1 June 2029.
#ASSERT `s 64A1(d)(1) — the last day to assess the shareholder, the company's assessment being made in` 2026 `and the shareholder's income assessable from` (YMD 2029 6 1) EQUALS YMD 2029 6 1
-- Assessable from 1 January 2028: 31 December 2028 is the later.
#ASSERT `s 64A1(d)(1) — the last day to assess the shareholder, the company's assessment being made in` 2026 `and the shareholder's income assessable from` (YMD 2028 1 1) EQUALS YMD 2028 12 31
-- Both on 31 December 2028: that day.
#ASSERT `s 64A1(d)(1) — the last day to assess the shareholder, the company's assessment being made in` 2026 `and the shareholder's income assessable from` (YMD 2028 12 31) EQUALS YMD 2028 12 31
